Build what a shell needs for an extensions page of its own.

A phone has no chrome://extensions it can use, so the shell draws the page
and asks the engine for what that page shows and does: the switched-off
extensions as well as the rest, enable and disable, uninstall behind
Chromium's own confirmation, the permission lines and site access, and the
options page. That lives in chrome/browser/ui/ohos/shell_extensions_ohos.cc,
an overlay file; this only adds it to the build next to the other shell
files.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after ohos-phone-tab-groups.patch.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
--- a/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
@@ -1731,5 +1731,7 @@
       "ui/ohos/shell_store_user_agent_ohos.h",
       "ui/ohos/shell_tab_groups_ohos.cc",
       "ui/ohos/shell_tab_groups_ohos.h",
+      "ui/ohos/shell_extensions_ohos.cc",
+      "ui/ohos/shell_extensions_ohos.h",
     ]
